# The repo's canonical text form is LF, enforced at checkout too: no smudge
# boundary between working tree and repo, so byte-level gates (verify-*
# comparisons, blob hashing, coverage offsets) see one form on every host.
# If a file class ever genuinely needs CRLF in the working tree (.bat/.cmd
# for cmd.exe), add a `*.bat text eol=crlf` override AFTER this line — the
# in-repo form stays LF; CRLF becomes checkout-time presentation only.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf binary

# Pairing records are generated from the three confirmed owner-blob pairs.
# The worktree-local installer registers the fail-closed driver command.
*.i18n.yaml merge=dsh-translation-pairing

# M-Bench fixtures: problem PDFs/attachments are frozen corpus, not source.
# The 490MB 2024-E csv is hashed in MANIFEST.json but not stored in git.
bench/problems/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bench/problems/**/*.xlsx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bench/problems/**/*.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# W8.10 handoff evidence: raw captures, exempt from the whitespace gate.
# These are verbatim records — provider outputs, terminal logs, and the
# archive files that quote audit detail character-for-character. Normalizing
# their whitespace would EDIT the evidence, which the round's own archive
# discipline forbids ("原样归档，不做美化"). The exemption is scoped to this
# round's directory on purpose: prose written BY hand (bench/*-REPORT.md)
# stays under the gate.
artifacts/handoff/W8.10/** -whitespace
